// src/main.rs
//
// Crate-level lint settings. We allow `dead_code` because this codebase
// has many intentionally-defined-but-not-yet-used items:
//   - Debug-derive struct fields that exist for diagnostic Debug output
//     but aren't read by code paths
//   - Public API surface kept available for future callers (e.g.
//     SecretBytes, log_summary::list_all, len() helpers on caches)
//   - Future-use enum variants, struct fields, and methods kept for
//     when a planned feature lands (e.g. EntityKind::File for upcoming
//     file-tracker pass, FilterStats fields for future analytics UI)
//
// Per-item #[allow(dead_code)] would be tidier but the warnings already
// number ~40 across 20 modules and growing. Crate-level allow keeps
// `cargo check` clean while we build out features.
//
// Removing this allow and addressing each warning individually is a
// future cleanup task. When ready, do it in a focused turn.
#![allow(dead_code)]

